---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/discount-strategy";
const title = "Shopify email discount strategy: govern the offer";
const desc = "For the retention operator and finance owner deciding who receives an incentive, what it costs and what happens when offers overlap. Begin with the promised offer and checkout rules before choosing a creative treatment.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Should every flow include a discount?",
    "answer": "No. Choose an incentive only when it serves a defined purchase obstacle and the economics support it."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does suppressing an email prevent code stacking?",
    "answer": "No. Inspect checkout combination and eligibility rules separately from message suppression."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should gift offers interact with a sale?",
    "answer": "Write a precedence rule that preserves the gift offer promise and check the resulting basket before sending."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should support receive?",
    "answer": "The offer version, recipient eligibility, expiry timezone, exclusions and a path for resolving failed redemption."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <article class="container prose-shopify py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl">{desc}</p>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Write an offer contract</h2><p>Give each offer an owner and record eligible products, audience, start and expiry timezone, combination rules, usage limits and exclusions. Match the signup promise, email, landing page and checkout. A reminder should not silently replace a promised welcome offer with a weaker one. Resolve that conflict before enrolling the customer.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Separate communication from enforcement</h2><p>An email eligibility branch controls who sees a message; it is not a checkout restriction. Document where the code is created and enforced, how expiry is calculated and what happens when it is shared. Verify the actual configured checkout behavior rather than assuming a tag or flow exclusion prevents redemption.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Choose value by product economics</h2><p>Compare a percentage discount with fixed value, shipping support, a bundle or no incentive. Include product cost, fulfillment, shipping subsidy and expected returns in the finance review. A higher-value cart does not automatically justify a deeper offer: bulky shipping or a low-margin line may consume the available contribution. Avoid universal cart-value ladders.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Resolve collisions explicitly</h2><p>Maintain an active-offer record with customer, offer version, source flow and expiry. Define what happens when a shopper with a welcome promise enters cart recovery during a public sale. Options include repeating the existing offer, sending a reminder without a new code or holding the promotional message. Record the chosen precedence and preserve the original promise. Do not assume every platform can share a real-time offer lock.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Proposed acceptance cases</h2><p>Test an eligible basket, an excluded item, a mixed basket, a previously redeemed code, an expired link and a customer with a simultaneous popup offer. For a proposed mixed-basket example, a sale board game and a full-price expansion should follow the written product rules at checkout; the email must not imply a basket-wide saving if only the expansion qualifies. These are proposed checks, not executed results.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Measure the decision, not only code use</h2><p>Separate issued, delivered, redeemed, cancelled and refunded orders. Define revenue and contribution consistently across incentive and no-incentive cohorts. Frequent redemption alone does not prove a customer would refuse full price. If running an experiment, define assignment, observation window and stopping rules in advance; do not interpret attributed orders as incremental profit.</p></section>
    <section class="py-6"><h2>Evaluate tools with the same offer</h2><p>Ask Sequenzy, Drip, Klaviyo or another candidate to demonstrate one written offer contract, its checkout enforcement, conflicting-flow handling and redemption export. Include the operator’s maintenance and support burden in the decision. This shortlist makes no ranking, current price or feature certification. Retire obsolete offer versions and preserve a support-readable explanation of what each recipient was promised.</p></section>
    <p>Continue with <a class="link" href="/use-cases/discount-strategy">discount strategy</a>, <a class="link" href="/use-cases/holiday-gifting">holiday gifting</a> or the <a class="link" href="/use-cases">workflow hub</a>.</p>
    <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Explore app candidates</a> · <a class="link" href="/compare">Compare requirements</a> · <a class="link" href="/for">Store-type guides</a></p>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Questions about this workflow" />
</BaseLayout>
